  "current_description_paragraph": "The 2009 direct assay uses six-His ASKA PfkA/FbaA, 2 µM enzyme, 5 mM S7P or F6P, 2 mM ATP and 50 mM potassium MOPS at 37 °C for 1 h (five samples). TableIII separates no-enzyme S7P 5.13±0.26 mM with products not detected; PfkA-only S7P 2.91±0.15/SBP 1.15±0.13; both enzymes S7P 3.05±0.14/SBP 0.79±0.11/DHAP0.23±0.02/E4P0.39±0.03; FbaA-only S7P 5.27±0.17 with products not detected; and the F6P comparison yielding FBP/DHAP but no detected E4P. No authentic SBP standard was available: migration reasoning and F1, 6BP calibration were used. Results report m/z369.0 and Methods367.0, an unresolved internal discrepancy rather than a silently corrected observation. [PMID:19756045]",
  "current_erroneous_phrase": "and the F6P comparison yielding FBP/DHAP but no detected E4P.",
  "independent_assessment": "F6P comparison column6 E4P is blank, defined as not determined. It is not an ND/no-detection result. No-metabolite column7 S7P, SBP, DHAP and E4P are all ND; only F6P/FBP are blank among the six detected-metabolite rows."
}
